{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws","id":851387,"title":"Metis Deformities, Merits and Flaws","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-22T15:16:39-07:00","id":851387,"title":"Metis Deformities, Merits and Flaws","content":"Has anyone ever created their own of any of these three? I just wanted to share some deformities I came up with and wouldn't shut-up until I shared them.<br /> <br /> <b>Prey Markings:</b> Your coat takes on the colors and markings of a prey animal (white tailed dear, racoon, etc). This causes others to look down on you for resembling the animals they hunt. Though there are some Metis whose coats can also resemble non-prey animals like foxes, dalmatians, tigers, etc, as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast Ears and Tail: </b>No matter what form you take, you will always have the ears and tail of a wolf. The wolf ears placed on top of the top of the head and can be covered with a turban, hijab or a large hairdo and tails can be tucked in, but they can still be a problem. Bastet Metis will have the ears and tails of whatever big cat they're from.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T15:44:29-07:00","id":851405,"title":"","content":"<b>Shark/fish teeth- </b>Instead of Warrior's fangs, you have one or more rows of sharp teeth in every form. This gives you a +diff to any social rolls, and -1 damage from any bite attacks you may do.<br /> <br /> <b>Gills-</b> You can, technically, breath underwater. In reality, you can process water through your gills for about an hour before you have to surface. Under duress or extending yourself, the time is halved. +2 diff on social rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Unnatural coat-</b> Blood Red. +1 Social diff to other garou.<br /> <br /> <b>Sloth Claws- </b>Your fingers are dull claws from the second digit onward. You have trouble using your hands at all.<br /> <br /> <b>Albino redux-</b> You have +2 diff on all sight rolls, and you take 1 bashing every hour you are in the sunlight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:13:53-07:00","id":851427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws?p=851405#post851405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shark/fish teeth- </b>Instead of Warrior's fangs, you have one or more rows of sharp teeth in every form. This gives you a +diff to any social rolls, and -1 damage from any bite attacks you may do.<br /> <br /> <b>Gills-</b> You can, technically, breath underwater. In reality, you can process water through your gills for about an hour before you have to surface. Under duress or extending yourself, the time is halved. +2 diff on social rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Unnatural coat-</b> Blood Red. +1 Social diff to other garou.<br /> <br /> <b>Sloth Claws- </b>Your fingers are dull claws from the second digit onward. You have trouble using your hands at all.<br /> <br /> <b>Albino redux-</b> You have +2 diff on all sight rolls, and you take 1 bashing every hour you are in the sunlight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unnatural Coat could also be fun with blue, green, pink or even purple colors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T17:01:28-07:00","id":851453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws?p=851427#post851427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unnatural Coat could also be fun with blue, green, pink or even purple colors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, or basically anything tied to spirits. I usually try to fit them to a theme, especially if the metis has spirit heritage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T17:36:54-07:00","id":851467,"title":"","content":"Conjoined twin who didn't change form, best npc ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T13:39:08-07:00","id":851980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws?p=851467#post851467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conjoined twin who didn't change form, best npc ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember seeing someone who had conjoined Black Spiral Dancer Metis twins. Except that they did go into Crinos form. Still that is an amusing idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T14:30:07-07:00","id":852020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws?p=851980#post851980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember seeing someone who had conjoined Black Spiral Dancer Metis twins. Except that they did go into Crinos form. Still that is an amusing idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they'd be stuck in crinos forever, as metis are born in that form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T18:13:12-07:00","id":852152,"title":"","content":"The Tail/Ear combo in all forms just screams to be used by &quot;furies&quot; and I wouldn't allow it in my games. <br /> I like Unnatural Coat, and Albino Redux. <br /> Sloth Claws starts off sounding like Fragile Claws, but than finishes ending up sounding like Club Hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T17:04:19-07:00","id":852676,"title":"","content":"<b>Feathers: </b>Your hair/fur is replaced with feathers just like a bird. (Eyebrows and body hair are just down.) While the feathers can be used in fetish creation, your unnatural appearance makes things very awkward (+1 social difficulty).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:48:45-07:00","id":854929,"title":"","content":"Something I've never or hardly seen in the books are &quot;Kinked Tail&quot; (<i>Fused tail bone vertebrae</i>) deformities for both the Garou and Bastet.<br /> Such a deformity would be more severe for a Bastet, as cats rely on their tails for balance and certain body language signals.<br /> It probably wouldn't be that much of a big deal among the Qualmi, who already have very short tails to begin with.<br /> <br /> The deformity results in either tails that are: short, very short, crooked, slightly bent, coily like a pig's tail, bent at a angle, bumps from fused bones, curved, mass etc.<br /> All depending on where the &quot;kink&quot; or fuse starts from in the tail.<br /> So you can have a tail that is mostly normal from the base and up, with the tip of the tail bent to a severe flat right or left angle due to the kink being there. So it looks like a upside down letter &quot;L&quot;.<br /> And fused bone vertebrae can also happen in the spine as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:01:19-07:00","id":854934,"title":"","content":"That would also make a pretty interesting battle scar, rather then just tail loss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T03:15:13-07:00","id":854962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws?p=854929#post854929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've never or hardly seen in the books are &quot;Kinked Tail&quot; (<i>Fused tail bone vertebrae</i>) deformities for both the Garou and Bastet.<br /> Such a deformity would be more severe for a Bastet, as cats rely on their tails for balance and certain body language signals.<br /> It probably wouldn't be that much of a big deal among the Qualmi, who already have very short tails to begin with.<br /> <br /> The deformity results in either tails that are: short, very short, crooked, slightly bent, coily like a pig's tail, bent at a angle, bumps from fused bones, curved, mass etc.<br /> All depending on where the &quot;kink&quot; or fuse starts from in the tail.<br /> So you can have a tail that is mostly normal from the base and up, with the tip of the tail bent to a severe flat right or left angle due to the kink being there. So it looks like a upside down letter &quot;L&quot;.<br /> And fused bone vertebrae can also happen in the spine as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the wolf use the tail to comunicate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6052-rettile-blitch","name":"Rettile&Blitch","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T19:04:53-07:00","id":855426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rettile&amp;amp;Blitch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws?p=854962#post854962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the wolf use the tail to comunicate <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said it's more severe for the Bastet (<i>Excluding the Qualmi.</i>). It doesn't just effect tail communication for them, but balance as well.<br /> Here's a <a href=\"http://www.americanexoticcats.com/breed-mutations.html\" target=\"_blank\">site/page with more detail on what they look like.</a> The same page also displays what Syndactyl and Polydactyl paws look like.<br /> <br /> I think that Metis should have the more extreme cases of really odd looking crooked tails than just ones with a slight bent to them.<br /> <br /> Other deformities for a Metis can be taken from this page on <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat_body-type_mutation\" target=\"_blank\">Cat-body type mutations</a>.<br /> <b>Munchkin </b>= Short limbs with both front and back legs. Makes it so you cannot make very long jumps or unable to use gifts like Leap of the Kangaroo<i>/</i>Hare's Leap.<br /> <b>Scottish Fold</b> = Very weak cartilage in the joints and ears. Not only does it make you look &quot;cute&quot; with the folded ears, but you have a hard time getting/moving around.<br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lykoi\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Lykoi</b></a> = (<i>Bastet Metis Only</i>) Your lack of a undercoat and odd fur makes you look slightly like a Garou or a wolf in a cat shaped form. Other Bastet distrust you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:50:37-07:00","id":855789,"title":"","content":"Metis deformities aren't supposed to be 'cute', damnit. You're missing the point. It's a debilitating condition to just be a metis, and having a really minor ailment just nulifies that. I wouldn't let my players ever take such joke deformities, unless they picked the two deformities flaw for a single point and the first one was actually a serious problem. You might as well add 'Homosexual' or 'Lactose intolerant' with some of the stuff you're putting up, yaoi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:12:46-07:00","id":855925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws?p=855789#post855789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis deformities aren't supposed to be 'cute', damnit. You're missing the point. It's a debilitating condition to just be a metis, and having a really minor ailment just nulifies that. I wouldn't let my players ever take such joke deformities, unless they picked the two deformities flaw for a single point and the first one was actually a serious problem. You might as well add 'Homosexual' or 'Lactose intolerant' with some of the stuff you're putting up, yaoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering the canon has such gems as Beastial Reflection or one ear, I'd say yaoi's are in line with the setting. Besides, I'd say most of these are meant to be taken together. For example, feathers+fish teeth+gills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T13:54:58-07:00","id":855975,"title":"","content":"I like the Lykoi idea, Laughing Hyena. That would result an odd looking bastet without being an over the top crazy mutant. The Lykoi breed is prone to molting too, so that could also present its own set of problems, physiological or social.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T23:33:57-07:00","id":856300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws?p=855789#post855789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis deformities aren't supposed to be 'cute', damnit. You're missing the point. It's a debilitating condition to just be a metis, and having a really minor ailment just nulifies that. I wouldn't let my players ever take such joke deformities, unless they picked the two deformities flaw for a single point and the first one was actually a serious problem. You might as well add 'Homosexual' or 'Lactose intolerant' with some of the stuff you're putting up, yaoi.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you are also addressing me because I added the &quot;cute&quot; word to the Scottish Fold deformity, but it is a really serious problem with the Scottish Fold cat breed.<br /> In fact, certain people are calling for the complete elimination of the Scottish Fold breed due to the fact it's genetic problems cannot be easily fixed compared to other breeds.<br /> <br /> This was a breed that was created because it looked &quot;Cute&quot; to people, but the features that made it look cute also impacted other parts of the body that most people aren't aware of. This stuff isn't &quot;minor&quot; either. The weak cartilage in the ears resulted in weak bones or weak cartilage in the rest of the body. That means they don't live as long compared to other breeds and often suffer horribly from movement in the joints.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://icatcare.org/advice/cat-health/scottish-fold-disease-%E2%80%93-osteochondrodysplasia\" target=\"_blank\">Would have been better just to call it &quot;</a><a href=\"http://icatcare.org/advice/cat-health/scottish-fold-disease-%E2%80%93-osteochondrodysplasia\" target=\"_blank\">Osteochondrodysplasia&quot;, which is often nicknamed &quot;Scottish Fold Disease&quot;, instead</a>?<br /> <br /> Some people also have issues with dog breeds like the Pug, French Bulldogs, Bulldogs, and other short snout dogs as well. Due to the fact that having such squished-in features results in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brachycephalic_syndrome\" target=\"_blank\">Brachycephalic Airway Obstruction Syndrome</a> and Brachycephalic Ocular Syndrome.<br /> <br /> Also, looking &quot;cute&quot; comes with it's own drawbacks in addition to problems caused by genetic mutations from it. You cannot be taken as seriously as other packmates and you might cause lesser delirium effects on humans. Or you might not cause the delirium to kick in at all, which would be a very serious issue","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T22:39:09-07:00","id":875317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws#post851387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone ever created their own of any of these three? I just wanted to share some deformities I came up with and wouldn't shut-up until I shared them.<br /> <br /> <b>Prey Markings:</b> Your coat takes on the colors and markings of a prey animal (white tailed dear, racoon, etc). This causes others to look down on you for resembling the animals they hunt. Though there are some Metis whose coats can also resemble non-prey animals like foxes, dalmatians, tigers, etc, as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast Ears and Tail: </b>No matter what form you take, you will always have the ears and tail of a wolf. The wolf ears placed on top of the top of the head and can be covered with a turban, hijab or a large hairdo and tails can be tucked in, but they can still be a problem. Bastet Metis will have the ears and tails of whatever big cat they're from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes i have come up with several.. 4 merits, 5 flaws, 2 new Archid Numina/Traits and one Metis Disfigurement.<br /> For the Metis Disfigurement, they can opt to have a banned form of the Opposite of their parentage.. So if both a garou's parents were Lupus, he can have 'No homid&quot; as his disfigurement..<br /> <br /> For Merits i have<br /> Gold Tolerance; Supernatural power, 7pt cost and/or 12pt cost. This is similar to Silver tolerance for Bastet and Garou, but is for Mokole and Corax. The 7pt power just allows soaking of gold, while the 12pt version allows soaking for BOTH gold and silver.<br /> <br /> Splinter of the minds Eye; 6 point cost or NONE (see write up), supernatural. This little known ability was supposedly a gift from Anubis to the Silent striders hundreds of years before the great exodus. It has several bonuses, but also a few downsides. For its bonuses, it Doubles the 'rank' of all stealth based powers/skills for purposes of what they are resisted with (IE if a nosferatu had it and had 3 dots in obfuscate, someone would need 6 or more in Auspex to see through). It also halves the cost to LEARN (not raise) new stealth based powers. Though its downside is it 'halves' the effective rating of search based powers for purposes for what it can penetrate (though the dice pool is not reduced) and also doubles the cost to learn NEW powers of a searching basis.<br /> Several Silent strider family bloodlines have this as an 'inherent' power, which costs them no points to take, but MUST be balanced out with taking the flaw Truth of Helios. <br /> <br /> Iron Skin; Physical, 3 points. This ability is often attributed to the martial art style Mui-thai, and is often called Maka-wara. It strengthens the skin to absorb impacts much easier. It doubles their stamina rating to soak BLUDGEONING melee/brawl attacks (though does nothing to improve soaking vs piercing or slashing attacks). Though someone possessing the merit can never have an 'unmodified by gift or power/shifted form&quot; appearance of higher than 2, and also imposes a -1 to -2 dice pool penalty for certain fine 'sensitivity' dexterous skills such as lock picking, or picking pockets.<br /> <br /> Spiritual attunement; Supernatural, 3 points. This merit makes it easier for mistics, star gazers and those with Chi to regain it by allowing them to roll their Willpower (Diff 9) to regain extra Chi/Gnosis when they are resting or doing certain activities to normally regain Chi/Gnosis. It also halves the XP to purchase new Gnosis or Chi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T23:01:02-07:00","id":875336,"title":"","content":"Cont..<br /> For Flaws i have<br /> Radiation; Physical 4 points. This flaw causes radiation detectors, Geiger counters etc to go off when the character is nearby (within 20 or so meters). No amount of scrubbing will block it, and a fine tuned enough sensor could potentially even be used to track them down if used within 2 hrs of a person's passing. For Mokole who have 2 or more slots in Huge size or other funky appearance numina/archid traits it actually is considered a 3 point Merit,<br /> as it allows them to not 'set off the delerium' (Man that gator is radioactive, must explain why he's so damn large boss)..<br /> <br /> Phlabolism; physical 5 points. This flaw is based on real life people who suffer from a lack platletts. When someone with this flaw is cut/slashed or pierced for 1 or more damage levels, they suffer 1 additional (unsoakable) point of damage each round until healed. Healing must take care of ALL the initial damage in one go. Fera with this can 'stop the blood loss by spending one full round doing no action, and making a successful Stamina check (diff 7, 2 or more successes needed).<br /> <br /> Truth of Helios; Supernatural. 4 points or free (see below). As with Splinter of the mind's eye this is a counter balance for that Merit for certain Strider families. All else must pay!.. Those who have this flaw though, have a very hard time telling lies. Though they at least will recognize any lie told TO Them (not just said in their presence). Any time they do try to tell a lie, their minds get wracked with pain and take one health level of lethal damage that can't be soaked. They have no issues with withholding information, OR coaching the answer in riddles or misdirections, its outright lies they can't say. <br /> <br /> Lack of common sense; Mental, 2 points or 6 points. Many players often play with having this flaw naturally in my experience! Those who possess the 2 point version can't ask for hints or advice on what to do from the Storyteller or other PCs if on their own (out of game questions though, such as would this or that skill be usable in x situation). If they take the 6 point version, the ST is encouraged to give bad/wrong advice/hints, or can ask for the spending of a willpower point to have 'come up with an idea' that common sense would have told them was a good idea....<br /> <br /> Oath of Osiris; supernatural, 5 points. This flaw is similar in some respects to Truth of Helios. When someone with this flaw ever signs a contract, makes an oath or gives a promise to do something, he is not just honor bound to do it, but 'supernaturally compelled to keep it. Any time he tries to break the oath/contract/promise, he suffers an immediate loss of 2 temporary willpower points, and needs to soak 2 lethal damage (Diff 8 to soak). If the person to which the oath/promise is given, does something on THEIR end to break it, the 'oath' is broken and the flaw owner can feel free to renig on his word. Death also breaks it in so far as long as said death was not in anyway caused/initiated by the oath giver..<br /> <br /> <br /> And lastly, 2 new Archid traits.<br /> Flame breath, 2pt. This trait is similar to acid spit and poison sacs, but is mutually exclusive in that having This prevents any of the other 2 from being taken (as is having any of them prevens this being taken). Once per week per permanent point of rage, the Mokole possessing this, can breath a gout of flame of 5 yards per combined point of Rage and Strength, dealing 5 dice of aggrivated damage (which can be increased on a 1 for one rage point basis). Those in the breath's area (45 degree arc) need to make a dodge roll against a 7 difficulty and get at least 3 successes to fully avoid it. If they only get 1 or 2 successes they have partially dodged it and only take 3 dice of damage. In the round the Mokole does this breath, they can not do any other action. Each week that goes by this trait is not used, the mokole can store up one additional 'breath' up to a maximum of 10 breaths period.<br /> <br /> Acid spitting, 2 points. Similar to flame breath it can't be combined with either of the other 2 but must be taken with the 'spittter' trait. It has a range (Straight line) equal to 2 yards per point of Rage and Str combined (Homid strength), and deals damage of 3 dice for initial impact, followed by 2 dice in the following round and finally 1 dice in the third round. To hit with it is Dex + Primal urge (diff 7) and it can be dodged normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:18:46-07:00","id":875602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/851387-metis-deformities-merits-and-flaws#post851387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone ever created their own of any of these three? I just wanted to share some deformities I came up with and wouldn't shut-up until I shared them.<br /> <br /> <b>Prey Markings:</b> Your coat takes on the colors and markings of a prey animal (white tailed dear, racoon, etc). This causes others to look down on you for resembling the animals they hunt. Though there are some Metis whose coats can also resemble non-prey animals like foxes, dalmatians, tigers, etc, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once ran a Changing Breeds one-shot LARP where one of the character options was a Silver Fang Metis named Uppatree whose Metis deformity was cat ears and tail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}